<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!-- UTINNI_WORLDMAP_FLIGHT_ICON_1 — the Utinni's own silhouette on the planet map.

       Vanilla (Odyssey, WorldObjectDefs/WorldObjects.xml) gives WorldObjectDef
       Gravship two textures and BOTH are on screen during a flight:
         <expandingIconTexture>World/WorldObjects/Expanding/Gravship</...>  zoomed out
         <texture>World/WorldObjects/Caravan</texture>                       zoomed in
       Patching only one leaves the ship changing shape as the player zooms, so both go.

       Texture binding is by texPath STRING, not by defName. The two paths below are the
       two PNGs in this mod's Textures/ tree and nothing else resolves them:
         Textures/World/WorldObjects/Expanding/RUT_Utinni.png
         Textures/World/WorldObjects/RUT_UtinniCaravan.png
       Both are 64x64, matching vanilla's own measured canvases for these two fields.

       Wrapped twice, and each wrapper earns its place:
       - PatchOperationConditional on the def, because Gravship is an Odyssey def and
         a bare Replace against an absent def logs a red error every load.
       - PatchOperationSettingGate (Source/PatchOperationSettingGate.cs) for the
         MOD_OPTIONS_RETROFIT_1 toggle "Utinni world-map icon". Off, no operation runs
         and the vanilla sprite is drawn — that is the graceful degradation.

       ⚠️ Gravship.ExpandingIconColor is a C# override returning the player faction's
       colour (RimWorld/Planet/Gravship.cs:146), so the sprite is MULTIPLIED by it and
       the XML expandingIconColor field is ignored. The art is authored near-neutral and
       value-led for that reason; do not "fix" the tint here, it cannot be fixed here. -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/WorldObjectDef[defName="Gravship"]</xpath>
    <match Class="RimMandrake.Utinni.UtinniPatches.PatchOperationSettingGate">
      <setting>utinniWorldIconEnabled</setting>
      <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
        <operations>

          <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
            <xpath>/Defs/WorldObjectDef[defName="Gravship"]/expandingIconTexture</xpath>
            <value>
              <expandingIconTexture>World/WorldObjects/Expanding/RUT_Utinni</expandingIconTexture>
            </value>
          </li>

          <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
            <xpath>/Defs/WorldObjectDef[defName="Gravship"]/texture</xpath>
            <value>
              <texture>World/WorldObjects/RUT_UtinniCaravan</texture>
            </value>
          </li>

        </operations>
      </match>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
